<Base
  title="About"
  subtitle="شازم (Shazim) means خوشی (khushi - happiness)"
  description="About Shazim: what the name Shazim means, and a design engineer's pursuit of work that uses all his talents and passions."
>
  <p>My name is pronounced SHAH-zim (<span lang="en-fonipa">/ˈʃɑːzɪm/</span>).</p>
  <p>
    For quite a while till my late teenage years, I didn't know what my name meant. Whenever my
    mother was asked what it meant she usually replied "Oh it was the name of a persian prince!". I
    have yet to find this persian prince, even AI can't. In the meantime, I can thank my sweet mom
    and grandfather, as well as the arabic and persian languages, for my unique name and its
    meaning.
  </p>

  <p>Do you know what your name means? Does it affect how you see yourself?</p>

  <hr />

  <p>
    My natural disposition is to speak in polymathematical abstracts, which has prompted many to
    call me a philosopher. In the modern world however, a philosopher is rarely given a place
    anywhere. So I'm currently working as a <a href="/work"> Design Engineer at Xbox</a> hoping to apply
    human-centric principles to create experiences that not only provide users what they value but do
    so with care.
  </p>

  <p>
    I am ever in pursuit of that <a
      href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ikigai#/media/File:Diagramo_de_Ikigajo_-en.svg"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"><i>ikigai</i></a
    > work path, that uses all my talents and passions optmially and most beneficially.
  </p>
</Base>
